<body>
    <div class="container">
        <h1>MasterPrompt Arts Privacy Policy</h1>
        <div class="meta">
            <strong>Last updated:</strong> 27 October 2026<br>
            <strong>App name:</strong> MasterPrompt Arts &nbsp;|&nbsp; <strong>Android package:</strong> com.abshixpro.app
        </div>

        <p>This policy explains what information the MasterPrompt Arts Android app collects, why it is collected, and who receives it. It is written so you can read it before you install the app, and so it can be published as the privacy-policy link in Google Play Console.</p>
        
        <div class="highlight-box">
            <p style="margin: 0;">If you do not agree with this policy, do not use the app.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>MasterPrompt Arts is an Android app for browsing AI image and video prompts, copying a prompt after you choose to, and, if you sign in, posting your own prompt photos and following other people.</p>
        <p>The editorial photos and videos in Discover are catalog content that we publish. They are not your private account data.</p>

        <h2>2. Information you give us</h2>
        <p><strong>Account:</strong> If you create an account or sign in, we use Google Firebase Authentication. We receive your email address, a Firebase user id, and (if you choose Google sign-in) the name and email address Google shares with the app. We use this only to sign you in, keep you signed in, and attach your community posts, likes, favorites, and follows to your account. We do not use Cloud Firestore.</p>
        <p><strong>Profile:</strong> If you add them, we store your username, profile title, and profile photo. Other signed-in users can see your username, title, profile photo, and the community photos you post.</p>
        <p><strong>Community posts:</strong> If you upload a photo, we store the photo file, the prompt text you type, keywords you type, the time of the post, and like/favorite counts on that post. You can delete your own community posts in the app, which removes them from your profile and the community feed.</p>
        <p><strong>Social actions:</strong> If you are signed in, we store community photos you like/favorite and users you follow/are followed by.</p>

        <h2>3. Information stored only on your device</h2>
        <p>These stay on your phone unless you clear the app’s storage:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Bookmarks and albums you create</li>
            <li>The app theme you choose</li>
            <li>Catalog text kept in memory while the app is open</li>
            <li>Profile photos cached for up to 30 days</li>
            <li>Videos you have played, cached for up to 7 days, then deleted automatically</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Advertising and Google AdMob</h2>
        <p>The app shows advertisements through Google Mobile Ads (AdMob), including banner ads, native ads, rewarded ads, and rewarded interstitial ads. AdMob may collect device identifiers (Google Advertising ID / AAID), IP address, approximate location, device model, OS version, and diagnostic info to serve ads, prevent fraud, and measure performance.</p>
        <p>For more details, review Google’s advertising privacy policies:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank">Google Privacy Policy</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" target="_blank">How Google uses data</a></li>
            <li><a href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543" target="_blank">AdMob Privacy Guide</a></li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Other services that receive information</h2>
        <p><strong>Firebase Authentication & Cloud Messaging:</strong> Used for secure sign-in and optional notification alerts when new photos are published (<a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank">Firebase Privacy</a>).</p>
        <p><strong>RevenueCat & Google Play Billing:</strong> Processes optional Pro subscriptions without storing your full payment card details (<a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy" target="_blank">RevenueCat Privacy</a>).</p>
        <p><strong>Content Delivery:</strong> Photos, videos, and catalog files load from <a href="https://prompts.masterprompt.art" target="_blank">prompts.masterprompt.art</a>.</p>

        <h2>6. How we use information</h2>
        <p>We use information to provide catalogs, authenticate accounts, manage community posts, send opted-in notifications, serve ads, handle Pro subscriptions, and maintain app security.</p>

        <h2>7. Your choices and rights</h2>
        <p>You can use Discover without an account, refuse sign-in or notifications, turn off ad personalization in Android settings, delete your own posts, or request account and data deletion by contacting us.</p>

        <h2>8. Contact</h2>
        <p>For privacy questions and data deletion requests, visit our contact portal at <a href="https://masterprompt.art" target="_blank">masterprompt.art</a>.</p>
    </div>
